# UI work gets a preview page

When the user asks for a UI implementation or a visible UI change (layout,
styling, map, cards, overlays, pin/popover, mobile chrome), add or update a
**preview page** in the same change. Do not leave the only way to see it as
“open production and find a listing.”

## Where

- Route: `/preview/<kebab-slug>` (e.g. `/preview/map-pins`)
- Register it on `/preview` (the index)
- `robots: { index: false, follow: false }`
- Not in production nav

## What the page must do

- Exercise the **changed interaction**, not only a static screenshot
- Use **fixture data** so it works without the listing database
- Name what changed in a short line at the top
- Put the preview URL in the PR body

Reuse `/intelligence/board-preview` and `/test` only when the work already
lives there. New UI work goes under `/preview`.
